('cor:multirow-size-switching','multirow-size-corollary multirow-mass-theorem current-term-rule-theorem','Set conditional. Its size count eliminates the need for H4 mass amplification, but it applies part(i), which still uses the affected H1 heavy-host avoidance bound. Thus the arithmetic |X_L| bound is retained while the per-reader round/switching probability remains conditional on a valid H1 replacement.'),
('thm:few-light-rows-switching','few-rows-theorem current-term-rule-theorem','Keep conditional. The large consistent-host mass branch K1 needs a justified matched-pair avoidance probability after exposure. Uniform residual-subset and rank estimates are separate. Decoder restoration only composes an independently justified p_R; it does not prove K1.'),
('thm:crowded-rows-exposed-switching','crowded-theorem current-term-rule-theorem','Keep conditional. Exposing crowded rows reduces to the recorded consistent-host and multirow probability arguments. The exposed-set construction/counting and conditional composition retain scope, but the affected avoidance/satisfaction estimates must be justified before the stated round or switching probabilities are used.'),
